### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 16 - UI ENDPOINTS, SETTINGS & ONBOARDING
###
### This file covers the remaining REST endpoints not tested in
### files 01-15: UI/status streams, settings management, onboarding
### wizard, and WebSocket token generation.
###
### Endpoint map:
###   GET    /api/v1/sessions/active           → active agent sessions
###   GET    /api/v1/agents                    → all agent statuses
###   GET    /api/v1/agents/events?sessionId=  → SSE agent state changes
###   GET    /api/v1/chat/stream               → SSE chat stream + heartbeat
###   GET    /api/v1/chat/stream/history/{id}  → chat message history
###   GET    /api/v1/hitl                      → paginated pending approvals
###   GET    /api/v1/hitl/events?sessionId=    → SSE HITL approval requests
###   POST   /api/v1/hitl/{taskId}/approve     → approve HITL by task ID
###   POST   /api/v1/hitl/{taskId}/reject      → reject HITL by task ID
###   POST   /api/v1/chat/ws-token             → get WebSocket auth token
###   GET    /api/v1/settings                  → current settings
###   GET    /api/v1/settings/prompt           → current system prompt
###   PATCH  /api/v1/settings/provider         → update LLM provider
###   PATCH  /api/v1/settings/prompt           → update system prompt
###   POST   /api/v1/settings/reset            → reset settings to defaults
###   GET    /api/v1/onboarding/status         → onboarding completion status
###   POST   /api/v1/onboarding/step/1         → start onboarding
###   POST   /api/v1/onboarding/step/2         → set provider + model
###   POST   /api/v1/onboarding/step/3         → set API key
###   POST   /api/v1/onboarding/step/4         → set system prompt
###   POST   /api/v1/onboarding/step/5         → configure MCP servers
###   GET    /api/v1/onboarding/complete       → finalize onboarding
###
### Note: SSE endpoints use EventSource (browser) or curl --no-buffer.
###       For VS Code REST Client, SSE responses stream until timeout.
###       WebSocket (/ws/chat) cannot be tested via .http files.
###
### Prerequisites: Amsha Agent running in serve mode, API key configured
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@validKey = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### A. UI & STATUS ENDPOINTS
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [UI-1] List all agent statuses (empty on cold start)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/agents
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [UI-2] Get active sessions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/active
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [UI-3] Create a session for UI tests
# @name uiSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "agentRole": "coordinator"
}

###

### [UI-4] Chat stream SSE - streams agent events + 20s heartbeat
### Note: This will stream until timeout. Use curl --no-buffer for CLI testing.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/chat/stream?sessionId={{uiSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [UI-5] Chat stream history - returns past messages for a session
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/chat/stream/history/{{uiSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [UI-6] Agent events SSE - live agent state changes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/agents/events?sessionId={{uiSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [UI-7] List pending HITL approvals (paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/hitl?page=0&size=20
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [UI-8] HITL events SSE - live approval requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/hitl/events?sessionId={{uiSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [UI-9] Get WebSocket auth token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/chat/ws-token
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{uiSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### B. SETTINGS ENDPOINTS
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [SETTINGS-1] Get current settings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SETTINGS-2] Get current system prompt
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings/prompt
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SETTINGS-3] Update LLM provider
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings/provider
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "provider": "groq",
  "model": "meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct"
}

###

### [SETTINGS-4] Update system prompt
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings/prompt
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "systemPrompt": "You are a helpful AI assistant."
}

###

### [SETTINGS-5] Reset settings to defaults
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings/reset
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SETTINGS-6] Settings without API key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings

###

### [SETTINGS-7] Prompt without API key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings/prompt

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### C. ONBOARDING ENDPOINTS (no API key required)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [ONBOARD-1] Check onboarding status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/status

###

### [ONBOARD-2] Start onboarding - Step 1
# @name onboardStep1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/step/1
Content-Type: application/json

###

### [ONBOARD-3] Step 2 - Set provider and model
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/step/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "groq",
  "model": "meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct"
}

###

### [ONBOARD-4] Step 3 - Set API key
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/step/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "apiKey": "gsk_test_key_for_onboarding"
}

###

### [ONBOARD-5] Step 4 - Set system prompt
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/step/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "systemPrompt": "You are a helpful AI assistant."
}

###

### [ONBOARD-6] Step 5 - Configure MCP servers
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/step/5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mcpServers": []
}

###

### [ONBOARD-7] Complete onboarding
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/onboarding/complete

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### D. HITL TASK-ID APPROVAL (new endpoint, different from session-based)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [HITL-TASK-1] Create session and trigger HITL
# @name hitlTaskSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "agentRole": "coordinator"
}

###

### [HITL-TASK-2] Run async to trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{hitlTaskSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
  "goal": "Look at the GitHub repository octocat/Hello-World and tell me what languages it uses",
  "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [HITL-TASK-3] List pending approvals to get taskId
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/hitl?page=0&size=20
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-TASK-4] Approve by taskId (replace TASK_ID with actual value from HITL-TASK-3)
### POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/hitl/TASK_ID/approve
### Content-Type: application/json
### X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}
###
### {}

###

### [HITL-TASK-5] Reject by taskId (replace TASK_ID with actual value)
### POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/hitl/TASK_ID/reject
### Content-Type: application/json
### X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}
###
### {}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{hitlTaskSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###
